    {
      "id": "source-062",
      "number": 62,
      "title": "LLaDA the big picture",
      "asset": "assets/slides/slide-062.svg",
      "sha256": "d7996df7a24fa107200d598568ca8bbf39d5aeb7fe1a33cc3cb9fd3659818240",
      "source_xml": "ppt/slides/slide62.xml",
      "source_xml_sha256": "c80c172aeac3e3c26ac9cf84763f1d5b8dbb7724a9adc539e4cb90b1066891bb",
      "paragraphs": [
        "LLaDA the big picture",
        "LLaDA is a masked diffusion model that follows standard pretraining and SFT while sampling via diffusion. ",
        "During pretraining, it masks all tokens randomly at ratio 𝑡∼𝑈[0,1] ; in SFT, only response tokens may be masked. ",
        "The model simulates diffusion from full masking (𝑡=1) to unmasking (𝑡=0), predicting all masks simultaneously at each step with flexible remasking.",
        "62"
      ],
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "id": "source-063",
      "number": 63,
